<title>USA: U.S. NAPM index 52.7 in Nov versus 50.2 in Oct.</title>
<headline>U.S. NAPM index 52.7 in Nov versus 50.2 in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>TEMPE, Ariz. 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Purchasing Management (NAPM) said on Monday its index of manufacturing activity rose to 52.7 in November from 50.2 in October. A listing of the main NAPM components follows:</p>
<p>		   Nov    Oct  Sept  Aug   July  June  May   April</p>
<p>PMI		52.7  50.2  51.7  52.6  50.2  54.3  49.3  50.1</p>
<p>Production     58.6  56.6  54.1  57.0  52.4  55.4  52.7  52.1</p>
<p>New Orders     55.4  51.6  56.3  55.6  54.0  61.3  52.4  53.8</p>
<p>Supplier Deliv 51.5  50.7  49.7  52.5  50.9  53.2  50.0  49.2 Inventories    41.8  38.9  44.8  41.6  41.2  42.3  38.3  44.6</p>
<p>Employment     47.5  45.5  46.9  48.2  45.5  49.4  45.5  45.3</p>
<p>Prices	   45.9  47.1  51.2  47.4  44.5  49.0  50.8  40.1</p>
<p>Export Orders  55.8  56.1  56.8  57.2  53.8  53.9  56.9  51.4 Imports	  52.5  53.8  51.8  50.6  53.7  48.6  49.8  46.2</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
